OL,3,CProgramme listings for WED 29 APR
OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GThe BBC Symphony Orchestra
OL,6,     Gconducted by Fabien Gabel in
OL,7,     GHerrmann, Blanchard, plus
OL,8,     GKorngold; and they premiere Ryan
OL,9,     GLatimer's Trumpet Concerto Bestia
OL,10,     Gwith soloist Selina Ott.
OL,11,G2145FThe Essay: The Death and Life of
OL,12,     FChristopher Marlowe
OL,13,     GJerry Brotton explores Marlowe's
OL,14,     Gtaboo-breaking play Edward II.
OL,15,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,16,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,17,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,18,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,19,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,20,     Geverything in between.
